Probably not, since for save/bones files to be
compatible, the size and organization of the
structures (C language "struct"s) they contain
have to be bit for bit compatible, and that is often
not just operating system and operating system
version dependent but also compiler and compiler
version dependent. If one save file's "char"
variables are 8 bits, and another save file's char
variables are 16 bits, for example, that is enough
to break save compatibility. Ditto 32 bit versus 64
bit integer variables, as is an issue right now for
MS-WinXP's two versions.

